report='''# R26 — world commands, registered loot, NPC consumables and message delivery

Parent GAME-EXE-EIREBUILD-ADDON-INTEGRATION-001 remains ACTIVE. Owner requested all remaining work together; this handoff is substantial progress, NOT fulfillment of that full request.48 additional command handlers were integrated, bringing available registry entries to91/93. CreateVoiceFX and CreateVoiceFXWait remain unimplemented. GetSkill(tame) still explicitly rejects its invalid reference array index. Handler counts do not measure overall addon transfer or complete gameplay parity.

Source work/eirebuild-local, branch/commit N/A copied engine snapshot. Reference57b8e0c42061a0acd51eaf64ea008aa1447d94ee, feature/world-background-data-20260916; unchanged installed-source provenance reused, exact files hashed in manifest. Local source changes only. No install, interactive launch, merge or push authorized/performed. Installed R8 and Starter route remain unchanged. No new runtime toggle.

## Implementation
MOB commands now cover player ownership, armor layers, object string IDs, distances, random values/strings/objects, object/group return dispatch, nearby-unit search, player GS variables, experience awards and notifications, party refresh, looting, game-over events, camera recording, chat/console, package file existence, unit flags/state, equipment damage/quick items, skill/cast/damage actions and zone departure. Native engine classes own these operations; no original EXE addresses or fake object store. GetUnitPose reads CUnitServer.currentPose.pose; fixture deliberately differs from CUnit.currentPose. Hero ID classification uses the reference threshold >=1000000000, not the narrower engine personage-name range. Empty equipment queries now assign empty string, as reference does.

Registered loot implementation adapted directly from RegisteredLoot.cpp: item validation/cache, duplicate occurrence counts, persistent per-zone/player item markers, consumed cleanup,5-segment activation delay,10-segment retry, actual native AddItemsToHoover, success-only save-load reconstruction and package/world lifecycle reset. Existing JMVRegisterLoot setting/defaultfalse retained. CLeverObject.ApplyScience reports successful activation. LeverApproach source behavior transferred through native objects: missing-model16-point ring, native route selection, stale point reset/rejection and actor/object proximity gate; authored models including zero-point records retain native interaction. No binary patch addresses.

NPC consumables implementation adapted from the complete reference consumable block in LuaScripts.cpp. Five kinds,3-bit charges, visit tokens, selection/phase persistence, effect-seen/effect-ended waits,109-segment healing cooldown, staggered4..7-segment polling and64-segment zone checks preserved. MOB registration defers to authoritative automatic Lua assignments and validates catalog/profile. Actual installed GetNpcCombatConsumableConfig supplies4 results; lookup cache not transferred yet. Native spell creation/self-cast, potion acknowledgment and visual event connected. Observer called on non-due regeneration ticks and after due resource commit; ordinary save-load and script restart call corresponding source lifecycle handlers. Runtime-only reset does not erase party GS markers. Existing always-enabled source behavior retained, no toggle introduced.

ShowMessage uses byte-identical ScriptMessageQueue: formatting/control validation,64-message bound, mutex/owner isolation and UI-only drain. Native mission Output Init binds, destructor unbinds/discards old messages, OnIdle appends through saved journal AddOutput and opens text mode. This transfers message delivery, NOT all NotificationPanel presentation: transient timeout, history/Escape behavior,50-line journal trimming and word measurement cache remain pending.

AckPotion issues the native server acknowledgment and client512 potion damage event. FlyingHitPoints renders the reference potion atlas rectangle (345/512,356/512,81/512) in white and suppresses zero digits for this event. Other new combat glyphs and full modified FlyingHP presentation remain pending.

## Confirmed source defects / deliberate adaptations
- DistancePointPoint registry said Fff but read4 floats. New text signature Fffff matches the source geometry formula; old two-argument compiled commands are rejected by arity checking. No claim of compatibility with malformed old serialized commands.
- CheckObjectFlag/CheckObjectFlag2 read objectParams[1] despite Ffo. Both now read the declared numeric argument; bit index constrained0..31. This fixes an invalid memory read, not an invented additional parameter.
- CastSomeSpellTarget removed unused coordinate reads including nonexistent floatParams[1]; actual target cast still uses its sole spell index and second object.
- Native server ProcessAttackPortion has3 arguments; reference facade supplied an extra -1. Bound to the actual native3-argument implementation; broader combat ABI/save parity unproved.
- Numeric/index safety adaptations from R25 retained. Missing objects/players are guarded where reference dereferenced them. Unknown script IDs still reach original engine, known unported commands fail explicitly.
- NPC_ReadPacked source rounded max24-bit float using float+0.5f, producing16777216 and invalid visit512. Boundary fixture exposed it. Round in double, preserving all valid integer bits and rejecting nonfinite input; persisted schema unchanged.

## Checks and observed limits
Final Build78 Release Win32 PASS; final check-world-commands-r26.py PASS; PE32 x86 and exact package copy identity PASS. Intermediate builds failed on native name/signature integration mistakes and fixture setup; only final artifact is delivered. A headless trace localized the fixture crash to SetUpdateMask on a referenced actor without a manager. Fixture now supplies its real native manager; production GetWorld semantics were not altered. Trace helper never uses --mod and creates no window; old interactive trace not run.

One final inspector includes previous native stats/regeneration/MOB/branch/binary script tests plus: four-argument distance parse/execute/export-reparse, equal-range Random, package path/traversal, empty group object return, real8-unit pose authority/state/flag/armor/ID queries, aggression mutation, high-bit marker, registered-loot codec/prefix rejection, message queue format/capacity/wrong-owner/teardown, NPC packed highest token/charges/selections/phases, and actual installed CyclopsA16 automatic strength profile plus absent-profile rejection. Intermediate failed packing test led to the source rounding fix. These checks do not execute all48 command actions.

Untested gameplay: populated proximity search, player/network events, real loot grant/removal/retry, lever navigation/obstruction, consumable application/charge exhaustion/effect visibility/save-load/zone visits, message UI and potion icon, damage and quest consequences. No game/UI/audio playback launched. No production3/3 or full original-addon save compatibility claim. Loot tests cover codec only, not grant transaction. NPC tests cover packing/config only, not full simulated world lifecycle or cast result. Invalid lookup Lua errors become explicit engine exceptions; original logged/rejected behavior differs. Native range searches currently follow source unit-only candidate list even when object flag is set; no invented broader enumeration.

## Remaining work and exact next step
CreateVoiceFX/Wait require Audio.cpp scenario/party voice routes and MiniaudioOneShotSfx.cpp playback ownership. Party-relative gain tracks the nearest living party member and world/zone identity; wait uses VoiceWaitState ticket publication and actual miniaudio voice end/cancel/pause lifetime. Merely using stock BeginFX or a timer would not transfer this contract. These2 handlers remain unavailable, not stubbed. Next source block: engine-owned audio backend adapters and voice lifetime bridge, then enable both IDs and test no-device/lifetime cases headlessly.

Broader parent still includes NPC equipment/spell migration, remaining tactical AI/death fear/murder awareness/combat/16-slot/client/interface/audio/network and fixes in FEATURE-MATRIX. Inventory statuses from early snapshots are not claims that these are now done. GetSkill(tame) intended data semantics unresolved. NotificationPanel/flying glyph work above is partial. Existing R17 startup/rendering defects remain queued for the final game phase. User has not changed the full goal or authorized gameplay yet.

Clean deliverable work/handoffs/eirebuild-x86-world-loot-consumables-20260916-r26 contains EXE, README, manifest. Exact matching PDB separately symbols/20260916-r26. Dependencies/game resources are not redistributed. Source preimages and transformed-source identities retained; no logs, saves or PDB in package. After complete source transfer, manual acceptance must exercise native MOB world commands, lever pickup, NPC consumption and save/load/zone transitions, voice completion/pause/cancel, message history and actual initial scene. Do not launch now. Merge/push not authorized.
'''
